    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for the owner endpoints. The request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner's `salutation` is derived at read time as `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the project's OpenAPI \u2192 MapStruct \u2192 OfficeFloor architecture (where derived fields like `displayName` and `initials` are computed in the mapper), the change spans:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `title` to the `OwnerFields` input schema (string, `MR|MRS|MS|DR`, stored & returned) and a read-only derived `salutation` to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 Added the `title` column field with getter/setter so the submitted title persists through POST \u2192 GET.\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added a `title` column to the `owners` table (the test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column is required; I updated all four for consistency).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `title` maps automatically by name both ways; added a `@Named(\"salutation\")` default method and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via `@Mapping`, mirroring the existing derived-field pattern.\n\nKept `title` as a plain string (rather than an enum) so MapStruct maps it to the `String` entity column without enum-conversion plumbing.\n\n**Result:** `AcceptanceTest` passes (`$.salutation` = `\"DR who\"`), and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
