    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- The `salutation` derivation sits alongside the existing `@Named` default methods (`displayName`, `initials`, `telephoneDisplay`, `locality`) in `OwnerMapper`, using the identical `@Mapping(..., qualifiedByName=...)` + `@Named` default-method pattern. The derivation logic lives in the right unit (read-time mapping, not the entity), consistent with how the other derived read-only fields are computed.\n- The `title` field on `Owner` follows the surrounding field/getter/setter convention (`@Column`, placed naturally among the other columns).\n- Schema changes are applied symmetrically across all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres), each in the same column position \u2014 no dialect left out, no duplication.\n- The OpenAPI additions mirror the existing property style (title/description/example, `readOnly: true` for the derived field).\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class or method is turning into a catch-all, and a maintainer would find the placement natural.\n\n(Non-structural aside, outside this review's scope: the OpenAPI `salutation` description says `'DR who'` while the example is `'DR Franklin'` \u2014 a doc typo, not a structural issue.)",
